cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the archived release and the
  accompanying article.
title: >-
  State-Generator Geometry: Geodesic Transport and Automatic Differentiation
  of the Levi-Civita Connection
type: software
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Bittner
    given-names: Eric R.
    affiliation: University of Houston
  - family-names: Silva-Acuña
    given-names: Carlos
    affiliation: Université de Montréal
repository-code: https://github.com/ebitnet65/JCP2b_State_Generator_Geometry_Code
abstract: >-
  Reference Python implementation for the state-generator geometry of an
  amplitude-damped optical Bloch model. The archive constructs the induced
  metric and two-form, evaluates the Levi-Civita connection symbolically and
  by automatic differentiation through a trace-constrained Liouvillian solve,
  validates the connection against finite differences, and computes a
  boundary-value geodesic between two control points.
keywords:
  - open quantum systems
  - state-generator geometry
  - geodesic transport
  - Levi-Civita connection
  - Christoffel symbols
  - automatic differentiation
